; ===========================================================================
; DLTX addon for Sych's trade file (zat_b30_owl_stalker_trader).
; Adds the artefact containers to his assortment.
;
; HOW THIS FILE IS LOADED
;   The engine opens its trade file by the path
;   configs\misc\trade\trade_zat_b30_stalker_trader.ltx, and while reading that
;   root file it automatically looks for "mod_<rootfile>_*.ltx" in the same
;   folder and picks up THIS file (Xr_ini.cpp:1138). So the file is loaded by
;   itself - no "#include" needed (including the base file would read it twice
;   and die with "Duplicate section 'trader'").
;
; WHY THE SECTION IS MARKED "!"
;   "[trade_generic_buy]" would declare a section that already exists -> the
;   engine dies with "Duplicate section ... wasn't marked as an override".
;   "![trade_generic_buy]" means "extend the existing section": our keys are
;   merged into it (Xr_ini.cpp:1067-1091).
;
; HOW EACH ENTRY MUST BE WRITTEN (the tricky part)
;   - A NEW key is a plain assignment:      bq_field_container = 1, 0.6
;     It creates the key in the section. A stale value from another addon would
;     be replaced, which is what we want for prices.
;   - The ">" prefix does NOT create a key: it APPENDS values to a key that
;     ALREADY exists in the section (Xr_ini.cpp:314-321 - if the key is not
;     found the whole entry is silently skipped). Our containers are absent from
;     the base trade lists, so ">bq_field_container" did nothing at all: the
;     trader paid full price and never had stock.
;   - ">" is only used below for "bq_container_base" which DOES exist in the
;     trade lists of the other addon: there we genuinely want to add to the
;     existing list rather than replace it.
;
; WHAT SYCH TRADES
;   Empty containers only. Combos (an artefact inside a container) have
;   can_trade = false, so they are neither offered nor bought.
;
; PRICES
;   The player BUYS an empty container for its full cost:
;     field 20000, universal 32000, scientific 45000, SIMK 13000.
;   The player SELLS it back at 60% (12000 / 19200 / 27000 / 7800) - the same
;   rate Sych buys artefacts at, so reselling is never profitable.
;
;   SIMK is cheaper on purpose: it cannot be worn on the belt, so it is a
;   portable container rather than a premium one.
;
; STOCK
;   "count, probability": each unit of a kind appears with its own chance.
;   Requested by the customer: field 50%, universal 20%, scientific 5%, and for
;   SIMK 1-3 units at 50% each.
; ===========================================================================

; What Sych pays the player.
;
; PRICE FORMULA (trade2.cpp:270-286):
;   price = cost * condition_factor * action_factor * get_buy_discount(trader_id)
;
; When the PLAYER SELLS to the trader, the engine uses the "buy" branch, i.e.
; the FIRST factor of this line (0.75), and get_buy_discount() multiplies it by
; the trader's discount section ("buy" value of [discount_1/2/3]). The discount
; depends on the player's standing ("+zat_b7_actor_really_helped_bandits
; +zat_b30_barmen_under_sultan" -> [discount_3], buy = 0.8), so with THAT
; discount the payout is 0.75 * 0.8 = 0.6 of the cost - exactly the 60% asked for:
;   20000 * 0.75 * 0.8 = 12000,  32000 * 0.75 * 0.8 = 19200,
;   45000 * 0.75 * 0.8 = 27000,  13000 * 0.75 * 0.8 = 7800.
; A single factor of 0.6 would NOT give 60%: 20000 * 0.6 * 0.8 = 9600, because
; the trader's standing discount multiplies it again.
; With a different discount ([discount_2] buy = 1 or [discount_1] buy = 1) the
; payout will be 0.75 * cost. The discount is the engine's own relation system,
; we do not change it here.
![trade_generic_buy]
bq_field_container = 0.75, 0.75
bq_uni_container   = 0.75, 0.75
bq_sci_container   = 0.75, 0.75
bq_simk_container  = 0.75, 0.75
; Аккумуляторы (пункт 5): Сыч принимает все пять классов в ЛЮБОМ состоянии,
; а цену движок сам уменьшает по заряду предмета - та же система, что у оружия
; (цена = cost * заряд * коэффициент * скидка за отношения).
; Значения: коэффициент для дружественных, для враждебных.
bq_battery_1       = 0.5, 0.4
bq_battery_2       = 0.5, 0.4
bq_battery_3       = 0.5, 0.4
bq_battery_4       = 0.5, 0.4
bq_battery_5       = 0.5, 0.4

; What Sych is willing to sell. The value is REQUIRED: an entry without a value
; is treated as "disabled" (CTradeParameters::process,
; trade_parameters_inline.h:125-128: empty value -> _action.disable), which is
; exactly how the base file marks artefacts it refuses to sell (they are listed
; as bare names with a ";NO TRADE" comment). Items the trader really sells are
; written with a value, e.g. "bandage = 1, 2.2" in [sell_tier_2].
![trade_generic_sell]
bq_field_container = 1, 1
bq_uni_container   = 1, 1
bq_sci_container   = 1, 1
bq_simk_container  = 1, 1
; Аккумуляторы Сыч продаёт новые (состояние 100%): предметы появляются в его
; ассортименте с зарядом из конфига, то есть 1.0.
bq_battery_1       = 1, 1
bq_battery_2       = 1, 1
bq_battery_3       = 1, 1
bq_battery_4       = 1, 1
bq_battery_5       = 1, 1

; Stock: count, probability. For SIMK the customer asked for 1-3 units, each
; with a 50% chance - that is "count 3, probability 0.5".
; Аккумуляторы: заказчик просил, чтобы шанс появления сильно падал с классом
; (батарейка чаще всех, экспериментальный - почти никогда).
![supplies_generic]
bq_field_container = 2, 0.5
bq_uni_container   = 2, 0.2
bq_sci_container   = 2, 0.05
bq_simk_container  = 3, 0.5
bq_battery_1       = 2, 0.5
bq_battery_2       = 1, 0.2
bq_battery_3       = 1, 0.05
bq_battery_4       = 1, 0.02
bq_battery_5       = 1, 0.005
